Iwidgets in bext
================

Bext packages Iwidgets 4.1.1 because Iwidgets is not bundled with Tcl or Tk
and cannot be assumed to be installed with a system Tcl/Tk stack.  The source
predates Itcl 4 and needs a small compatibility patch when used with the Itcl
4.1.1-or-newer stack required by BRL-CAD.

Upstream status
---------------

The latest official Incr Widgets source release is 4.1.1.  The release archive
and bext's generic widget sources match except for expanded CVS Id strings;
bext omits obsolete build, CVS, demo, manual, and test files and supplies its
own CMake packaging.  The Tcl Core fossil project named "iwidgets for itk4"
has only two check-ins, both from May 24, 2012, and its source retains the
compatibility defects fixed here.  There is consequently no newer maintained
upstream source to import as of September 2026.

Tcl can discover versions advertised by system package indexes without loading
Iwidgets or opening a display.  That is sufficient for inventory, but not for
safe selection: an unpatched system package and one with equivalent downstream
fixes both advertise version 4.1.1.  Loading enough code to validate behavior
also loads Tk and requires a display.  Bext therefore continues to use its
known patched copy by default instead of treating the version string as proof
of compatibility.

Compatibility patch
-------------------

Itcl 3 accepted an array element as the argument to itcl::scope.  Itcl 4
instead resolves that argument as a variable name and rejects array element
syntax.  The patch resolves each common array's fully qualified variable name
with namespace which, then appends the element index.  This preserves the
variable names expected by Tk -variable, -textvariable, trace, and tkwait
without depending on Itcl 3's itcl::scope behavior.

The Finddialog match callback previously constructed a command with subst and
then executed the resulting string.  Tcl 8.5's argument expansion syntax
invokes the stored command prefix directly, preserving argument boundaries and
supporting the command prefixes produced by Itcl 4.

Labeledwidget::alignlabels originally passed the unqualified class name
Labeledwidget to itcl::find.  Itcl 4 resolves that name in the caller's object
context.  The result therefore depended on package initialization order: it
worked when Itcl was loaded before Tk, but failed in applications such as
bwish and Archer where Tk was initialized first.  The patch uses the fully
qualified ::iwidgets::Labeledwidget class name so both supported initialization
orders behave identically.

Panedwindow's frame hull shares its resource class name with Tk's native
panedwindow widget, whose event bindings call a different widget API.  The
patch removes that class tag from the hull's binding list while retaining
Iwidgets' configure and sash bindings and the Panedwindow resource class.
Pointer motion and clicks therefore use the correct handlers without
changing native Tk panedwindow behavior.

These changes are kept as a bext patch rather than modifications to the source
submodule.  That keeps the imported upstream revision identifiable and makes
the compatibility delta explicit and independently reviewable.  The external
project patches a staged copy so builds do not modify the source submodule.

Validation
----------

The BRL-CAD Tcl/Itcl smoke baseline exercises the affected Iwidgets under both
initialization orders:

* btclsh loads Itcl before Tk and represents command-line tools such as
  rtwizard;
* bwish initializes Tk before tclcad loads Itcl and represents Archer and
  other Tk-first applications.

The baseline constructs and operates the affected widgets, invokes
Labeledwidget::alignlabels, follows callbacks after returning to the event
loop, and treats background Tcl errors as failures.  Xmin supplies the X
server needed to run the GUI case on headless builders.
